  ('jackson-hole-wyoming', '12A', 'Jackson Hole', 'United States', 'Ride Big Red to the top of America''s steepest', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Greater Yellowstone', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","romance","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["JHMR = Teton Village, WY; INDEPENDENT (Kemmerer family since 1992); on the FULL Ikon Pass ONLY (not Base/Session) + ALL Ikon holders must make advance lift reservations (days may sell out)","Base 6,311 / summit 10,450 ft (Rendezvous Mtn); VERTICAL 4,139 ft (one of the biggest in the US); 2,500 in-bounds acres + ~3,000 backcountry-access; terrain ~10% beg / 40% int / 50% expert; ~450+ in snow; no night skiing","The Aerial Tram ''Big Red'' (100-pax, ~9 min, current tram Dec 2008) climbs to Rendezvous; Corbet''s Cabin summit waffles; CORBET''S COULOIR = expert chute with a committing ~10-20 ft cornice entry, then an expert run (not a sustained death-pitch)","Jackson Hole Airport (JAC) = the ONLY commercial airport inside a US national park (Grand Teton); ~7 mi N of Jackson town, ~28 min to Teton Village; RESORT (Teton Village) is distinct from the TOWN of Jackson (~12 mi)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: high-visitation/high-spend/capacity-constrained (Ikon reservations + sell-outs) but no per-resort count published - consensus only","Guiding + heli are INDEPENDENT, NOT resort-run: Jackson Hole Mountain Guides (AMGA-accredited, est. 1968) for backcountry/AIARE; heli via a separate third-party outfitter (operator unverified); NO resort cat/heli","A two-national-park basecamp: Grand Teton adjacent + Yellowstone ~1.5 hr N; National Elk Refuge (~25,000 ac, ~7,500 elk, winter sleigh rides); big summer season","NO natural hot springs at Teton Village (Granite Hot Springs - winter snowmobile access; Astoria Hot Springs - reservations; both day-trips); Ikon/lift prices dynamic; Amangani closed for refurbishment (verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"St. John''s Health, 625 East Broadway, Jackson (~12 mi from Teton Village) - full-service 24/7 ER; higher-level trauma out of valley (trauma level verify)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base 6,311 ft, summit 10,450 ft - tram tops 10,000 fast; hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if AMS worsens); AVALANCHE life-safety spine (in-bounds patrolled/controlled; boundary gates + ~3,000 ac backcountry severe) - Bridger-Teton Avalanche Center (BTAC), Tetons zone (also Snake River/Salt River & Wyoming Ranges/Togwotee) - confirm zone label; beacon/probe/shovel + guide (JHMG), never duck ropes; CORBET''S + steep chutes = no-fall zones (committing entries; respect closures); TETON PASS (WY-22, summit 8,431 ft, Glory Bowl slide paths) - WYDOT early-morning avalanche-control closures, >60 mi detour when closed; tree-wells; cold + intense UV; keep wildlife distance in the parks","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week, Feb-Mar) - capacity-pressured (Ikon reservations, sell-outs); + big summer national-parks peak (Jun-Aug)","shoulder":"early Dec (pre-holiday) + late-Mar/early-Apr spring skiing","green":"mud season (mid-Apr-May) + late fall (Nov) - between winter + national-parks seasons","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Four Seasons/Amangani/Caldera House 4-8 mo (holidays longer); summer parks far ahead; full-Ikon lift reservations seasonal","off_season_specials":"spring skiing; whole summer Grand Teton/Yellowstone season; fall wildlife/elk; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Preside